  "description": "Where does the number of table occurrences in one query stop being accepted, and at which phase? Only the count varies (n = 16, 32, 33, 34, 50) over aliases of the one-row table ONE: a comma cross join, and a nest of parenthesized INNER JOINs on x. Each text is opened directly with the standard capture. Runs on a fresh copy of r-sql-13b-main (ACCDB) opened read-only through ACE DAO; each text is opened as a snapshot with Database.OpenRecordset, Fields Name/Type/Size are read before the first row, then every row's Field values to EOF (each MoveNext captured), then Close and DBEngine.Errors.",
